# Security Guidelines

**Focus**: Comprehensive security practices for Laravel + Vue 3 + Inertia.js applications
**Goal**: Prevent vulnerabilities before they reach production
**Approach**: Defense in depth with multiple layers of security

## Mandatory Security Checks

Before ANY commit:

- [ ] No hardcoded secrets (API keys, passwords, tokens)
- [ ] All user inputs validated (Form Requests on backend, Vue validation for UX)
- [ ] SQL injection prevention (Eloquent ORM, parameterized queries)
- [ ] XSS prevention (Vue auto-escaping, sanitized v-html)
- [ ] CSRF protection enabled (Laravel default, Inertia automatic)
- [ ] Authentication required (auth middleware)
- [ ] Authorization verified (policies, gates)
- [ ] Rate limiting on all endpoints (throttle middleware)
- [ ] Error messages don't leak sensitive data
- [ ] Mass assignment protection ($fillable/$guarded on models)
- [ ] File upload validation and sanitization (mimes, max size)
- [ ] No exposed .env file in version control
- [ ] APP_DEBUG=false in production

## Secret Management

### PHP/Laravel

```php
<?php

// ❌ NEVER: Hardcoded secrets
$apiKey = "sk-proj-xxxxx";

// ✅ ALWAYS: Environment variables
$apiKey = config('services.openai.key');
// or
$apiKey = env('OPENAI_API_KEY');

if (!$apiKey) {
    throw new \RuntimeException('OPENAI_API_KEY not configured');
}
```

### TypeScript/JavaScript

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER: Hardcoded secrets
const apiKey = 'sk-proj-xxxxx';

// ✅ ALWAYS: Environment variables
const apiKey = import.meta.env.VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY;

if (!apiKey) {
    throw new Error('VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY not configured');
}
```

### Environment File Security

```bash
# .env - NEVER commit this file!
APP_KEY=base64:xxxxx
DB_PASSWORD=secret123
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxxxx

# .env.example - Safe to commit (no real values)
APP_KEY=
DB_PASSWORD=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
```

## Laravel Security Best Practices

### SQL Injection Prevention

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: Eloquent (automatic parameter binding)
$markets = Market::where('status', $status)->get();

// ✅ GOOD: Query Builder with bindings
$markets = DB::table('markets')
    ->where('status', '=', $status)
    ->get();

// ✅ GOOD: Raw queries with parameter binding
$markets = DB::select(
    'SELECT * FROM markets WHERE status = ?',
    [$status]
);

// ✅ GOOD: Named parameter binding
$markets = DB::select(
    'SELECT * FROM markets WHERE status = :status',
    ['status' => $status]
);

// ❌ NEVER: String concatenation
$markets = DB::select("SELECT * FROM markets WHERE status = '$status'");
```

### XSS Prevention

```php
<?php

// In Blade templates:

// ✅ GOOD: Automatic escaping with {{ }}
<h1>{{ $market->name }}</h1>
<p>{{ $user->comment }}</p>

// ⚠️  CAUTION: Raw HTML with {!! !!} - only use for trusted content
<div>{!! $trustedHtmlContent !!}</div>

// ✅ GOOD: Use Laravel's e() helper in PHP
echo e($userInput);

// ✅ GOOD: Use htmlspecialchars() in pure PHP
echo htmlspecialchars($userInput, ENT_QUOTES, 'UTF-8');
```

### CSRF Protection

```php
<?php

// Laravel automatically includes CSRF protection for:
// - All POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE routes
// - Forms rendered with @csrf Blade directive
// - Inertia.js requests (automatic)

// In Blade:
<form method="POST" action="/markets">
    @csrf
    <!-- Form fields -->
</form>

// In Inertia.js (automatic):
form.post('/markets', data); // CSRF token automatically included
```

### Mass Assignment Protection

```php
<?php

namespace App\Models;

class Market extends Model
{
    // ✅ OPTION 1: Whitelist fillable attributes
    protected $fillable = [
        'name',
        'description',
        'category',
        'end_date',
        'creator_id',
    ];

    // ✅ OPTION 2: Blacklist guarded attributes
    protected $guarded = [
        'id',
        'is_admin',
        'resolved_at',
    ];

    // ❌ NEVER: Empty guarded (allows all)
    // protected $guarded = [];
}

// Safe usage:
Market::create($request->validated()); // Only validated fields
Market::create($request->only(['name', 'description'])); // Specific fields

// ❌ UNSAFE: Using all request data
// Market::create($request->all());
```

### Authorization with Policies

```php
<?php

namespace App\Policies;

use App\Models\Market;
use App\Models\User;

class MarketPolicy
{
    /**
     * Determine if the user can update the market.
     */
    public function update(User $user, Market $market): bool
    {
        return $user->id === $market->creator_id;
    }

    /**
     * Determine if the user can delete the market.
     */
    public function delete(User $user, Market $market): bool
    {
        return $user->id === $market->creator_id
            || $user->is_admin;
    }
}

// In Controller:
public function update(UpdateMarketRequest $request, Market $market)
{
    // ✅ Authorize before action
    $this->authorize('update', $market);

    $market->update($request->validated());

    return back();
}
```

### File Upload Security

```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Http\UploadedFile;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Storage;

public function uploadAvatar(Request $request)
{
    // ✅ GOOD: Validate file uploads
    $request->validate([
        'avatar' => [
            'required',
            'file',
            'image',                    // Only images
            'mimes:jpeg,png,jpg,gif',   // Specific types
            'max:2048',                 // Max 2MB
            'dimensions:min_width=100,min_height=100,max_width=2000,max_height=2000',
        ],
    ]);

    $file = $request->file('avatar');

    // ✅ GOOD: Generate safe filename
    $filename = $file->hashName(); // Generates unique, safe name

    // ✅ GOOD: Store securely
    $path = $file->store('avatars', 'public');

    // ❌ NEVER: Use original filename
    // $file->storeAs('avatars', $file->getClientOriginalName());

    return $path;
}
```

### Rate Limiting

```php
<?php

// In routes/web.php or routes/api.php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\RateLimiter;

// ✅ Route-level rate limiting
Route::middleware(['auth', 'throttle:60,1'])->group(function () {
    Route::post('/markets', [MarketController::class, 'store']);
});

// ✅ Custom rate limiter (in App\Providers\RouteServiceProvider)
RateLimiter::for('api', function (Request $request) {
    return Limit::perMinute(60)->by($request->user()?->id ?: $request->ip());
});

// ✅ Conditional rate limiting
RateLimiter::for('markets', function (Request $request) {
    return $request->user()?->is_admin
        ? Limit::none()
        : Limit::perMinute(10)->by($request->user()->id);
});
```

### Password Security

```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Hash;

// ✅ GOOD: Hash passwords
$user->password = Hash::make($request->password);

// ✅ GOOD: Verify passwords
if (Hash::check($plainTextPassword, $user->password)) {
    // Password matches
}

// ❌ NEVER: Store plain text passwords
// $user->password = $request->password;

// ✅ GOOD: Password validation rules
$request->validate([
    'password' => [
        'required',
        'string',
        'min:8',
        'confirmed',        // Requires password_confirmation field
        Password::min(8)
            ->letters()
            ->mixedCase()
            ->numbers()
            ->symbols()
            ->uncompromised(), // Check against data breaches
    ],
]);
```

### Secure Session Configuration

```php
<?php

// config/session.php
return [
    'driver' => env('SESSION_DRIVER', 'database'),
    'lifetime' => 120,              // 2 hours
    'expire_on_close' => false,
    'encrypt' => true,              // ✅ Encrypt session data
    'http_only' => true,            // ✅ Prevent JavaScript access
    'same_site' => 'lax',          // ✅ CSRF protection
    'secure' => env('SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE', true), // ✅ HTTPS only
];
```

## Vue/Frontend Security

### XSS Prevention in Vue

```vue
<template>
    <!-- ✅ GOOD: Vue automatically escapes -->
    <div>{{ userInput }}</div>
    <div>{{ market.name }}</div>

    <!-- ⚠️  DANGEROUS: v-html - only use with trusted content -->
    <div v-html="trustedHtmlContent"></div>

    <!-- ✅ GOOD: Sanitize before rendering -->
    <div v-html="sanitize(userHtml)"></div>
</template>

<script>
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';

export default {
    methods: {
        sanitize(html) {
            return DOMPurify.sanitize(html);
        },
    },
};
</script>
```

### Preventing CSRF in Inertia.js

```typescript
// Inertia automatically includes CSRF token in all requests
// from the meta tag in app.blade.php

// No additional configuration needed!
form.post('/markets', data); // CSRF token included automatically
```

### Secure API Calls

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Use Inertia for authenticated requests
import { router } from '@inertiajs/vue3';

router.post('/api/markets', data); // Includes auth cookies

// ✅ GOOD: For external APIs, secure the token
const response = await fetch('/api/markets', {
    headers: {
        Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
        Accept: 'application/json',
    },
});
```

## Common Vulnerabilities (OWASP Top 10)

### 1. Broken Access Control

```php
<?php

// ❌ BAD: No authorization check
public function delete(Market $market)
{
    $market->delete();
    return back();
}

// ✅ GOOD: Authorize action
public function delete(Market $market)
{
    $this->authorize('delete', $market);
    $market->delete();
    return back();
}
```

### 2. Cryptographic Failures

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: Use Laravel's encryption
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Crypt;

$encrypted = Crypt::encryptString('sensitive data');
$decrypted = Crypt::decryptString($encrypted);

// ❌ NEVER: Roll your own crypto
// $encrypted = base64_encode('sensitive data');
```

### 3. Injection Attacks

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: Always use parameter binding
$users = DB::table('users')
    ->where('email', $email)
    ->get();

// ❌ NEVER: String concatenation
// $users = DB::select("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '$email'");
```

### 4. Insecure Design

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: Implement proper authentication
Route::middleware(['auth'])->group(function () {
    Route::post('/markets', [MarketController::class, 'store']);
});

// ✅ GOOD: Implement authorization
$this->authorize('create', Market::class);
```

### 5. Security Misconfiguration

```php
<?php

// config/app.php
'debug' => env('APP_DEBUG', false), // ✅ False in production

// .env
APP_ENV=production
APP_DEBUG=false
```

## Error Handling Security

```php
<?php

// ✅ GOOD: Generic error messages to users
try {
    $market = Market::create($data);
} catch (\Exception $e) {
    Log::error('Market creation failed', [
        'user_id' => auth()->id(),
        'error' => $e->getMessage(),
        'trace' => $e->getTraceAsString(),
    ]);

    // Don't expose internal details
    return back()->withErrors([
        'message' => 'Failed to create market. Please try again.'
    ]);
}

// ❌ BAD: Exposing internal details
catch (\Exception $e) {
    return back()->withErrors([
        'message' => $e->getMessage() // Might expose sensitive info
    ]);
}
```

## Logging Security Events

```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;

// ✅ Log security-relevant events
public function login(Request $request)
{
    if (Auth::attempt($request->only('email', 'password'))) {
        Log::info('User logged in', [
            'user_id' => auth()->id(),
            'ip' => $request->ip(),
        ]);

        return redirect()->intended();
    }

    Log::warning('Failed login attempt', [
        'email' => $request->email,
        'ip' => $request->ip(),
    ]);

    return back()->withErrors(['email' => 'Invalid credentials']);
}
```

## Security Testing

### Backend Security Tests (PestPHP)

```php
<?php

use App\Models\User;
use App\Models\Market;

// ✅ Test authentication required
test('guest cannot create market', function () {
    post('/markets', [
        'name' => 'Test Market',
    ])->assertRedirect('/login');
});

// ✅ Test authorization
test('user cannot update another users market', function () {
    $owner = User::factory()->create();
    $otherUser = User::factory()->create();
    $market = Market::factory()->create(['creator_id' => $owner->id]);

    actingAs($otherUser)
        ->put("/markets/{$market->id}", [
            'name' => 'Hacked',
        ])
        ->assertForbidden();
});

// ✅ Test mass assignment protection
test('user cannot set is_admin via mass assignment', function () {
    $user = User::factory()->create();

    actingAs($user)
        ->put("/profile", [
            'name' => 'New Name',
            'is_admin' => true, // Should be ignored
        ]);

    expect($user->fresh()->is_admin)->toBeFalse();
});

// ✅ Test rate limiting
test('rate limiting prevents abuse', function () {
    $user = User::factory()->create();

    // Make 61 requests (assuming 60/min limit)
    for ($i = 0; $i < 61; $i++) {
        $response = actingAs($user)->post('/markets', [
            'name' => "Market {$i}",
        ]);
    }

    expect($response->status())->toBe(429); // Too Many Requests
});
```

### Frontend Security Tests (Vitest)

```typescript
import { mount } from '@vue/test-utils';
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import MarketForm from './MarketForm.vue';

describe('MarketForm Security', () => {
    it('escapes user input by default', () => {
        const wrapper = mount(MarketForm, {
            props: {
                market: {
                    name: '<script>alert("XSS")</script>',
                },
            },
        });

        // Vue should escape the script tag
        expect(wrapper.html()).not.toContain('<script>');
        expect(wrapper.html()).toContain('&lt;script&gt;');
    });

    it('disables submit button during processing', () => {
        const wrapper = mount(MarketForm);

        // Simulate form processing
        wrapper.vm.form.processing = true;

        const button = wrapper.find('button[type="submit"]');
        expect(button.attributes('disabled')).toBeDefined();
    });
});
```

## Security Audit Commands

### Quick Security Check

```bash
# Run all security checks
composer audit && npm audit && php artisan test

# Check for secrets
rg "password|api_key|secret|token" app/ resources/js/ --ignore-case

# Check for SQL injection risks
rg "DB::raw|DB::statement|DB::select" app/

# Check for mass assignment risks
rg "create\(\$request->all\(\)|update\(\$request->all\(\)" app/

# Check for XSS risks
rg "v-html|innerHTML" resources/js/

# Check .env is ignored
git ls-files | grep "^\.env$"
```

### Comprehensive Security Audit

```bash
# Backend
composer audit
./vendor/bin/phpstan analyse app --level=max
./vendor/bin/pint --test

# Frontend
npm audit --audit-level=high
npm run type-check
npm run lint

# Routes
php artisan route:list

# Check for debug mode
grep "APP_DEBUG" .env
```

## Security Checklist for Pull Requests

### Before Submitting PR

- [ ] Run `composer audit` (backend dependencies)
- [ ] Run `npm audit` (frontend dependencies)
- [ ] Run `php artisan test` (all tests pass)
- [ ] Check for hardcoded secrets with grep/rg
- [ ] Verify .env changes are in .env.example only
- [ ] Review code for security vulnerabilities
- [ ] Test authentication/authorization manually
- [ ] Test rate limiting on new endpoints
- [ ] Verify input validation on all forms

### During Code Review

- [ ] Check for SQL injection vulnerabilities
- [ ] Check for XSS vulnerabilities (v-html, innerHTML)
- [ ] Verify authorization checks (policies, gates)
- [ ] Verify input validation (Form Requests)
- [ ] Check file upload security (if applicable)
- [ ] Verify error messages don't leak data
- [ ] Check mass assignment protection
- [ ] Verify rate limiting on new routes
- [ ] Check session configuration (if changed)
- [ ] Verify HTTPS enforcement (if changed)

## Security Configuration Checklist

### Laravel Configuration

```php
// config/app.php
'debug' => env('APP_DEBUG', false), // ✅ Must be false in production
'key' => env('APP_KEY'),           // ✅ Must be set and unique
'url' => env('APP_URL', 'https://example.com'), // ✅ Use HTTPS

// config/session.php
'secure' => env('SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE', true), // ✅ HTTPS only
'http_only' => true,                            // ✅ No JS access
'same_site' => 'lax',                          // ✅ CSRF protection
'encrypt' => true,                              // ✅ Encrypt session

// config/cors.php
'allowed_origins' => [env('FRONTEND_URL')],     // ✅ Specific origins
'allowed_methods' => ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'], // ✅ Explicit
'allowed_headers' => ['*'],
'credentials' => true,                          // ✅ Allow cookies

// config/auth.php
'passwords' => [
    'users' => [
        'expire' => 60,        // ✅ Tokens expire in 60 minutes
        'throttle' => 60,      // ✅ Rate limit password resets
    ],
],
```

### Environment Variables (.env)

```bash
# Application
APP_ENV=production          # ✅ Set to production
APP_DEBUG=false            # ✅ Disable debug mode
APP_KEY=base64:...         # ✅ Generated key
APP_URL=https://yourdomain.com # ✅ Use HTTPS

# Database
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=your_database
DB_USERNAME=your_user
DB_PASSWORD=strong_password # ✅ Strong password

# Session
