SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE=true # ✅ HTTPS only

# Mail
MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=noreply@yourdomain.com
MAIL_FROM_NAME="${APP_NAME}"
```

## Security Monitoring

### What to Log

```php
<?php

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Log;

// ✅ Log security events
Log::info('User logged in', ['user_id' => auth()->id(), 'ip' => request()->ip()]);
Log::warning('Failed login', ['email' => $email, 'ip' => request()->ip()]);
Log::error('Unauthorized access attempt', ['user_id' => auth()->id(), 'resource' => $resource]);

// ❌ Don't log sensitive data
// Log::info('User login', ['password' => $password]); // NEVER!
// Log::info('Payment', ['credit_card' => $cc]);      // NEVER!
```

### Events to Monitor

- Failed login attempts (potential brute force)
- Multiple password reset requests (potential account takeover)
- Unauthorized access attempts (403 Forbidden responses)
- Rate limit exceeded (429 Too Many Requests)
- SQL errors (potential injection attempts)
- File upload failures (potential malicious uploads)
- Large payload sizes (potential DoS attack)
- Unusual API usage patterns

